3	import java.util.Locale;
4	
5	/**
6	 * The single definition of an owner's {@code identityKey}: the one derived value that all
7	 * duplicate detection is expressed through. It is
8	 * {@code normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId}, where the
9	 * telephone is normalized to E.164 via {@link OwnerTelephones} (so a stored value and a
10	 * freshly created one compare the same way), the email is lower-cased (empty when absent)
11	 * and the householdId is used as-is (empty when the owner is not in a shared household).
12	 *
13	 * <p>Two owners collide only when their WHOLE keys are equal. Because the telephone is part
14	 * of the key, two members of the same household (same householdId) with different telephones
15	 * have different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.
16	 *
